    {
      "title": "Sleeve checks and no smartglasses: South Korea races to protect all-important university exams against AI",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/south-korea-university-entrace-exams-ai-cheating-measures",
      "description": "<p>South Korea has been gripped by revelations of AI-aided cheating, just days before more than half a million students are to sit high-stakes entrance exams</p><p>The integrity of South Korea’s career-defining university entrance exam has been thrown into doubt after the top scorer in a recent professional exam <a href=\"https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/technology/2026/nov/15/ai-cheating-south-korea-college-entrance-exam\">admitted using a concealed camera</a> and AI to cheat.</p><p>On Thursday, more than half a million people, mostly school students, are due to sit the exam, known as the suneung, at 1,312 centres across the country. The exam runs for a gruelling eight hours over a single day and determines which university a candidate can attend and, in turn, their future prospects.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/18/south-korea-university-entrace-exams-ai-cheating-measures\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-18T02:03:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "South Korea offers $75,000 bounties to catch AI-assisted exam cheats",
